So when we're doing these reactions,
the first thing that we need to do

00:01:02.505 --> 00:01:06.095
is when it comes to the steps is
balancing the chemical equation.

00:01:06.535 --> 00:01:10.205
So sometimes this may involve
predicting the chemical equation.

00:01:10.515 --> 00:01:14.264
The good news is that most
solution equations typically are

00:01:14.264 --> 00:01:16.114
double replacement reactions.

00:01:16.580 --> 00:01:21.170
So, you're going to be doing that inside
outside bonding together, and balancing

00:01:21.170 --> 00:01:25.030
them usually is some of the easier
types of ones to balance, especially

00:01:25.030 --> 00:01:28.330
when you compare them to combustion,
